Research probe: bank $7F read watch (archived, not maintained)

Logs every 16-bit guest read from WRAM bank $7F (or every bank with
SNESRECOMP_READ_WATCH_ALL=1) with frame, address, value, CPU registers and the
recompiled call stack. It was used to find how the game reads the unpacked
track table (native-map spike, "Read-watch evidence: multi-segment row
assembly", and the track-format decode). It was removed from the build by
openspec change uniracers-code-cleanup-2 because it sat on the guest RAM read
path.

Switches: SNESRECOMP_READ_WATCH_FILE=<path> (required),
SNESRECOMP_READ_WATCH_FRAME_MIN / _MAX, SNESRECOMP_READ_WATCH_ALL.

Apply from game/snesrecomp/:
    git apply ../../tools/patches/research/read-watch.diff
Revert with git apply -R. Written against framework pin 9c6afcb plus the local
patch (game/patches-snesrecomp-local.diff); it may need refreshing after a
framework update.

